Flintlock Toboggan is a fiend kept in the [[Sigzil Haight|Shackled Prince's]] demesne. He's about 4'6", humanoid, covered in short brown fur. He has hooved feet, and a goatlike face with human features. He has two curled rams' horns protruding from his forehead, and his pupils are hourglass shaped instead of round.

He is chained by the arms and legs with black metal chains cut with runes, in a small room of [[Geography/The Quorum|the Quorum]] on the [[Geography/Star 221,325|Joker World at Star 221,325]]. The chains burn him when he reaches for magic. He says they cannot hold him: if he is killed, he only reforms in the chains. He says he was sealed there by [[Sigzil Haight]] after trying to take the prince's place.

He bargains for his freedom. He offered the Scale delvers whatever they wanted in exchange for his release, or a riddle to solve for a smaller prize, and he kept his word when they solved the second riddle and took two crankshafts. They left him chained and locked the door. He called after them that they would be back, and that he had the true name of [[Org/The Scale/People/Manuel de la Cruzada|Reverend Warden Manuel de la Cruzada]] and would come for him once free.
